    "dict1": {
      "a": 1,
      "b": 2
    },
    "dict2": {
      "b": 3,
      "c": 4
    }
  }
}
```

The `merge_dictionaries` function takes two dictionaries as arguments and returns a single dictionary that contains all the key-value pairs from both dictionaries. In this case, the resulting dictionary will be:

```json
{
  "a": 1,
  "b": 3,
  "c": 4
}
```

Note that the value of key 'b' in the resulting dictionary is the value from `dict2`, as it is the last dictionary provided to the function.

